    "historicalContext": "Cadillac used the São Paulo weekend to reset Pérez's power-unit allocation after the issue that ended his Mexico City race, fitting a new ICE, turbo and MGU-K before a clean, dry FP3; the subsequent qualifying deficit was therefore not another carry-over reliability interruption. In a rain-delayed Q1, both cars briefly sat inside the top 16 on full wets, but Pérez lost tyre temperature for his final lap while Bottas's rear tyres overheated after initially switching on quickly. Their P20/P21 classification should consequently be read as a late-window tyre-temperature and execution loss in Cadillac's first wet qualifying of the season, while Pérez's component changes also committed him to a back-of-grid start.",
